WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:07.181
Rey training scenes, a showdown between BB-8
and BB-9E, a crazy Porg moment, and Poe and

00:00:07.181 --> 00:00:11.690
Finn in Canto Bight, are just some of the
many deleted scenes from Star Wars: The Last

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:12.690
Jedi.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:16.330
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and today I'm revealing and explaining a stack

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:19.550
of cut scenes and rejected concepts from Episode
8.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:24.420
Although The Last Jedi is the longest movie
in the Star Wars saga so far, director Rian

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.619
Johnson has confirmed there's at least half
an hour of deleted scenes and even more unused

00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:32.890
footage and he's promised there will be plenty
of extra scenes on the Blu-ray.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:37.079
Just before I get into that, I'm starting
a second round of my Star Wars giveaway.

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:40.620
To enter, make sure you're a subscriber and
leave me a comment with your thoughts about

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.770
the deleted scenes.

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:44.620
I'll announce the winner of the first round
later in the video.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:49.430
Oh, and if this is your first time on my channel,
I do regular deleted scenes videos, movie

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:52.110
breakdowns, easter eggs, theories and giveaways.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:56.640
Quick spoiler warning, I'll be discussing
scenes from The Last Jedi in detail, so take

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.399
care if you've not watched it yet.

00:00:59.399 --> 00:01:03.429
Let's start on Ahch'To where Rian Johnson
has confirmed there was a huge scene cut which

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:07.590
showed Rey performing a type of additional
trial and then a very emotional scene between

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:09.049
Rey and Luke afterwards.

00:01:09.049 --> 00:01:14.270
Now, if you remember, Luke told Rey he'd teach
her three lessons, but in the movie we only

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:18.940
saw her complete two of those before she decided
to leave the island to try and turn Kylo Ren

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:20.140
to the light side.

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:24.280
Which makes me think the third lesson was
going to be the trial or test that was cut

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:25.280
from the movie.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:29.600
There's some incredible artwork in the Art
of The Last Jedi book which shows Rey facing

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:34.381
off against two figures or visions which resemble
Darth Vader and Obi Wan Kenobi, the choice

00:01:34.381 --> 00:01:35.381
of the light and the dark side to Rey.

00:01:35.381 --> 00:01:38.020
The fact that Rey's standing in water here
suggests it could be an alternate version

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:42.780
of the mirror scene in the movie, with Luke
having told Rey to enter the island's Cave,

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:47.620
just as Yoda told Luke to enter the Dark Side
Cave on Dagobah in The Empire Strikes Back.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:51.549
And other concept art also seems to indicate
that the cave scene might have explored the

00:01:51.549 --> 00:01:55.750
duality of the light and the dark side in
addition to Rey's parentage as it did in the

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:56.750
movie.

00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:01.020
Other possibilities for Rey's deleted training
scene include footage from the trailer and

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:04.880
behind-the-scenes reel of her running with
a lightsaber on the beach.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:08.350
Concept art of this scene shows that Rey was
running towards the Caretaker village where

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:10.240
you can see some fires.

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:14.240
And in another piece of concept art, Rey and
Luke are on a cliff where they spot marauders

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:18.750
approaching the village, which makes me think
maybe the village was attacked and Rey attempted

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:19.750
a rescue.

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:23.610
Alternately, the fires in the village might
be from a scene that looks like a Caretaker

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:27.850
celebration, which means Rey's beach run could
be showing her training while the island's

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:30.910
inhabitants are enjoying themselves.

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:34.450
Concept art also indicates there could have
been a scene of Rey practising her skills

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:38.490
with numerous training remotes which could
have been fun to see.

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:42.770
An old training remote popped up in The Force
Awakens when Finn picked it up on the Millennium

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:47.070
Falcon, and seeing Rey in a scene like this
could have been a nice call back to Episode

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:51.390
4 when Luke briefly used one to train with
Obi Wan Kenobi.

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:55.660
There's also a separate deleted and extended
sequence with Rey and the Caretakers.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:59.880
The Art of The Last Jedi book reveals that
one particular Caretaker, the matron, "has

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:04.620
a problem with Rey being on the island, [as]
Rey [is] intruding in this private world,

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.880
and in this private relationship that they
have with Luke."

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:11.110
There was a little allusion to this deleted
scene in the film when Rey mentioned to Luke

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:13.191
that she didn't think the Caretakers liked
her.

00:03:13.191 --> 00:03:17.010
And there's a load more unused concept art
featured in the Art of book.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:21.850
Some of my favourites include Luke and Rey
on a skiff on their way to the old Jedi temple

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:25.510
which in this version was carved into the
side of the island.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:29.010
Another cool shot had Rey accessing the temple
via a cliff.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:33.020
And in this version of the Jedi temple, the
entrance was specifically designed to resemble

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:37.250
the window behind the Emperor's throne in
Return of the Jedi, the idea being to show

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:43.040
that the early symbols of the Jedi have been
used by both the light and the dark sides.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:46.600
After Finn wakes up towards the start of the
film, there's a deleted scene where he finds

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.790
out what happened while he was unconscious.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:53.180
Basically, BB-8 plays a hologram of Rey's
scene in The Force Awakens where she kisses

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:56.270
Finn on the forehead and says "We'll see each
other again".

00:03:56.270 --> 00:04:00.340
It's interesting this was deleted because,
in The Last Jedi, Finn has a brief romantic

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:03.150
moment with Rose after she saves him on Crait.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:07.230
And later in the Millennium Falcon, you can
see Rey looking at Finn while he takes care

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:08.850
of Rose.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:13.550
BB-8 also had another deleted scene where
he squared off against his evil counterpart

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:15.250
BB-9E.

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:19.820
Creature effects creative supervisor Neal
Scanlan told EW that The Last Jedi would feature

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:25.260
"a lovely moment between BB-8 and BB-9E, which
[would tell a] sort of parallel story of Vader

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:26.320
and Luke."

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:30.940
We did get that pretty insane moment of BB-8
commandeering a First Order walker on the

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:36.220
Supremacy, and some scenes of BB-8 and BB-9E
together did appear in a Last Jedi-themed

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:40.430
ad for Verizon, but it was a shame we didn't
get a showdown between these two droids in

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:41.450
the actual movie.

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:47.480
The story on Canto Bight was changed significantly
numerous times during The Last Jedi's development.

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:51.330
Initially, that part of the movie was going
to feature Finn and Poe Dameron, rather than

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:53.130
Finn and Rose Tico.

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:56.710
When Rian Johnson reviewed his early script
though, he discovered that Finn and Poe's

00:04:56.710 --> 00:05:01.370
story in the wealthy casino city wasn't exciting
enough because there was no conflict between

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:04.520
the two characters as, in some ways, they
were too alike.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:08.880
So, Poe was replaced with Rose, who challenges
Finn and therefore allows his character to

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:11.150
develop during the course of the film.

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:15.250
Interestingly, in early drafts, Finn was also
going to be part of the Resistance fighter

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:16.770
squadron in the opening battle.

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:21.340
In fact, he was going to be on the same ship
as Rose's sister, Paige, and actually witness

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:22.340
her death.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:26.601
However, Rian Johnson pulled the plug on this
part of Finn's story when he realised that

00:05:26.601 --> 00:05:31.550
including a big scene where Finn had to reveal
this to Rose would slow the movie down.

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:36.060
Even after the story settled on Rose and Finn
in Canto Bight, there were still several more

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.510
changes to that part of the movie.

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:42.780
Originally, after arriving in the city, the
pair were going to break into a shop to steal

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:46.640
a gown and tuxedo so they'd blend in better
in the casino.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:51.090
Additionally for Rose, putting on the gown
was going to be a kind of transformation moment

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:53.840
from her practical Resistance overalls.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:57.920
And a tuxedo-clad Finn was going to enjoy
getting a lot of attention in the casino,

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:01.950
until he discovered he'd put on his tux back-to-front.

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:05.870
After this scene was deleted, Finn and Rose's
lack of disguise meant they were easy to spot

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:09.400
and apprehend, so they never got to meet the
Master Codebreaker.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:14.340
Rian Johnson also had an important storyline
planned for the Master Codebreaker, which

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:16.130
sadly we didn't get to see.

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:20.710
In a deleted subplot, Finn and Rose would
have made contact with him after he finished

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:25.990
playing the piano and singing with a female
alien on stage in the casino's cabaret room.

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:29.810
After talking with him, they would have learned
that he was on the trail of an insectoid warlord

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:31.680
called the Butcher of Brix.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:35.730
The Codebreaker planned to steal the jewels
that paid for the warlord's brutal regime,

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:39.960
but along with Rose and Finn, he would have
ended up caught by the Canto Bight police

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:43.710
on the casino rooftop, trying to break into
the warlord's room.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:48.340
And there's more deleted scenes for Finn and
Rose when they get on board Snoke's Supremacy

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:50.120
to find the hyperspace tracker.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:55.030
Rian Johnson told Collider there's an extended
sequence of Finn, Rose and DJ sneaking through

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:59.139
the Mega Star Destroyer until they arrive
at a "big office area […] and then [have]

00:06:59.139 --> 00:07:03.860
to fake out [some] Stormtroopers", which sounds
to me like it could be a hat tip to Han and

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.450
Luke in A New Hope.

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:09.180
There's also some concept art which hints
at some of the moments and visual jokes we

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:10.870
might have seen in this sequence.

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:15.450
In one of them, Finn and Rose come across
masses of lint in a tunnel, which they follow

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:20.290
along till they fall through a trap door into
a huge tumble-dryer in the First Order laundry

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:21.300
room.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:24.730
This scene sounds as if it could have been
reminiscent of the trash compactor scene in

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:30.100
Episode 4 and was probably also a joke at
Finn after he threw Phasma in a trash compactor

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:32.180
in The Force Awakens.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:36.270
Another piece of concept art then has Rose
and Finn facing off against what they think

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:42.370
is a bunch of Stormtroopers, in a moment evocative
of Han Solo in A New Hope, but in this case,

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:47.110
the Stormtroopers are actually revealed to
be just empty suits on a dry-cleaning rack.

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:51.580
We did get that funny moment in the movie
with the First Order laundry and iron droid

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:56.620
gag, which felt like a nod to the 1978 Star
Wars parody, Hardware Wars; and I think these

00:07:56.620 --> 00:08:00.330
deleted scenes would have formed part of that
moment.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:04.830
Concept art also depicts unused scenes of
Finn and Rose running down a "power converter

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:07.560
hallway" on The Supremacy after they're discovered.

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:11.639
The pair were going to end up in a classic
Star Wars-looking scene on a narrow bridge

00:08:11.639 --> 00:08:13.610
with an enormous chasm beneath.

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:17.330
In the end though, the scene was rejected
as Rian Johnson considered it too "on the

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.330
nose".

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:22.820
There's still much for us to learn about Snoke
which I'm hoping will be answered in Episode

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:27.320
9, but there was a small deleted moment with
the Supreme Leader in The Last Jedi.

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:31.830
In the cut scene, Snoke would have delivered
a line about his gold slippers, which I imagine

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:35.620
would have fit in with what the Visual Dictionary
says, that he wears them because his physical

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:38.479
frailties cause him to prioritise comfort.

00:08:38.479 --> 00:08:44.080
Back on the Jedi Temple island, those little
Porg critters initially had some rather freaky

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:46.090
multi-coloured designs.

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:49.920
And if you thought that scene with Chewie
and a roasted Porg was a bit dark, there's

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:53.760
actually a piece of concept art of a Porg
being impaled by a lightsaber!

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:57.280
It looks like this would have occurred during
the scene when the little creatures were playing

00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:58.990
with Luke's abandoned lightsaber.

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:03.260
I doubt there was much chance this would have
made it in to the movie, but if it had, it

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:07.700
would have foreshadowed the way Kylo Ren took
out one of Snoke's Praetorian Guard, with

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:09.890
a lightsaber right through the head.

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:14.520
By the way, if you're wondering whether any
Leia scenes were deleted, Rian Johnson has

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:17.730
only said that no major scenes with Carrie
Fisher were cut.

00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:22.020
However, there were some smaller moments cut
that didn't quite work with the final movie.

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:26.390
And actually, I talk about how Leia's deleted
scenes could be used to complete her arc in

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:30.740
Episode 9 in my Carrie Fisher video, which
you can tap in the top right to watch or click

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:33.060
the link in the video description.

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:37.020
Now, what did you think about these deleted
scenes and are there any you wish had been

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:38.380
included in the movie?

